From: LIS Code Agent <leolin84200704@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 16:41:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [VP-18185] validateSampleId: report upstream gRPC outage as
 503, not "Sample not found"

A dead EMR/core gRPC target used to surface to accessioning as HTTP 404
"Sample not found with input id", so a service outage was worked as if the
clinic had never placed the order (Zendesk 754019).

- validateSampleId: map upstream-unreachable errors (grpc UNAVAILABLE /
  DEADLINE_EXCEEDED, or the wrapped message forms) to 503 with an explicit
  "not confirmation the sample is missing" message; genuine misses keep 404.
- getSampleIdByEmrOrderId: retry only transport failures (bail on a
  deterministic found=false instead of 3 pointless retries) and keep the
  grpc status code on the wrapped error.
- New spec covering the 503/404 split on both the sample_id and
  emr_order_id paths, including the 10-digit id reroute.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
